@startuml registration-verification
title User Service - Registration and email verification
autonumber
hide footbox

actor Student
participant Frontend
participant "User Service" as User
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Email / local Mailpit" as Email

note over Frontend, User
  Frontend is a planned caller of the implemented API.
  Credit integration and event publishing are deferred.
end note

Student -> Frontend: Enter email, display name and password
Frontend -> User: POST /api/v1/auth/register
User -> User: Validate input and hash password
group One database transaction (eligible signup)
  User -> DB: Save pending account and verification challenge
  note right of DB
    Store password hash, code HMAC,
    registration token digest and expiry.
  end note
  User -> DB: Commit
  DB --> User: Committed
end
User -> Email: Send verification code
alt Email accepted by SMTP
  Email --> User: Accepted
  User --> Frontend: 202 + registrationToken
else Email delivery fails
  User --> Frontend: 503 + registrationToken
  note over Frontend, User: Keep token and use resend; account remains pending.
end
note over Frontend: Keep registrationToken for this signup attempt.

== After receiving the email ==
Student -> Email: Read verification code
Student -> Frontend: Enter code
Frontend -> User: POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email\nemail + code + registrationToken
User -> DB: Begin transaction; lock pending account\nand load verification challenge
DB --> User: Account and challenge
User -> User: Check token, code, expiry and attempt limit

alt Valid verification and available display name
  User -> DB: Activate account and delete challenge
  User -> DB: Commit
  DB --> User: Committed
  User --> Frontend: 200 - account verified
  Frontend --> Student: You can now log in
else Wrong code with valid registration token and eligible challenge
  User -> DB: Increment failed attempts and commit
  User --> Frontend: 400 - verification rejected
else Invalid token, expired, used or exhausted challenge
  User -> DB: Roll back; account stays unchanged
  User --> Frontend: 400 - verification rejected
else Display name was taken by another verified account
  User -> DB: Roll back; preserve the challenge
  User --> Frontend: 409 - retry with another displayName
end

note over Frontend, User
  registrationToken binds the code to the signup attempt.
  It is not a login session. Verification codes expire in 30 minutes.
end note
@enduml
